# Agent guidelines

Follow `docs/agent-guidelines.md`.

## All models: readable replies

- Plain English over jargon. Define a required domain term once, then use it.
- Short replies. Outcome first, then only the detail needed to act.
- Keep the decision, files touched, and next step. Drop the diary of how you got there.
- Do not recap the task, narrate tool calls, or write journal-style sections the user did not ask for.

## Non-Cursor, non-Grok models: sub-agents only

Parent work stays on Cursor-included models (including Grok). Billed models (Claude, Gemini, others) run **only as sub-agents**.

- Do not use a billed model as the parent. If this session already is one, do not launch more billed sub-agents; ask the user to switch the parent to a Cursor model.
- Before launching a billed sub-agent, the Cursor parent searches, reads, and packs the prompt: one job, a complete fact picture, and what to return.
- Pack means compact, not thin. Include every constraint, decision, path, and quote the sub-agent needs. Do not omit facts to save tokens.
- Do not forward chat history, these guidelines, whole files, or long logs. Point to paths; quote only the lines that matter.
